 ## Understand the implementation
 
+The loop awaits the registered context provider after input admission and header/context logging, passing the original derived messages and the prepared call. It appends the selected messages and optional native prefix as `request/projection`, then requires a successful persistence flush before dispatch. Cancellation, provider replacement, or changed source history during selection or flush rejects the attempt. Without a provider, the loop clears any previous projection and uses ordinary history. It deep-freezes selected message identities and freezes the request array and envelope while keeping cancellation live; native prefix data comes from the recorded projection.
+
