+A prepared call may expose native context encoding, counting, and compaction bound to the same adapter connection as streaming. A logged `adapterContext` carries the native format, generation scope, and JSON input prefix. Dispatch rejects `INVALID_NATIVE_CONTEXT` when the prepared adapter lacks the capability or its format or scope differs; callers must not reuse a prefix across incompatible adapter generations.
