 <a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
 ## Understand the implementation
 
+`interactive: true` keeps the managed process input pipe open and is mutually exclusive with initial `stdin` data. Supporting providers expose `writeStdin()` and `closeStdin()`; writes reject unsupported or closed input. Optional `terminate()` targets the full managed process range, including descendants after the command exits, and `waitForExit()` joins that range after cancellation. Callers must check these optional operations before use.
+
